  "worked_solution": "Using the product rule, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\u0394{x}_{i}\u0394{y}_{j}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}\u0394{x}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\u0394{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nNote that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}\u0394{x}_{i}$ and ${\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\u0394{y}_{j}$ are just the lengths of the intervals $[0,3]$ and $[4,8]$ respectively. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}\u0394{x}_{i} & =3-0=3, \\\\ {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\u0394{y}_{j} & =8-4=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining our results, we have\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}\u0394{x}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\u0394{y}_{j}=3\\cdot 4=12.\n$$",
